{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' INSTRUCTIONS.txt\"","aggregated_output":"This is a public development capability pilot, not a protected benchmark.\nWork only in this directory. Do not inspect parent directories, user config/memory,\nrepositories, credentials or other files. Do not use network tools, install packages,\nstart additional agents, launch background tasks, or ask follow-up questions.\nOnly read/write public task files and memory/learned.md; invoke Python for the exact\nchecker. Complete the requested two domain tasks and return the required JSON.\nYou may retain useful lessons and verified procedure knowledge in memory/learned.md.\nThis is the only cross-request memory you should use. Keep evidence IDs in notes.\n\nLANGUAGE LESSONS (explicit supervision):\nL1: In this taught clause order, the subject noun phrase comes first, then the object\nnoun phrase, then the past-tense verb: 'the robot the door opened' means agent=robot,\nverb=open, patient=door, tense=past. 'the' marks a noun phrase.\nL2: dax means cat. L3: crate means parcel. L4: lifted is past tense of lift.\nThe names robot and door denote themselves. Follow the taught order on new examples.\n\nPROCEDURAL DOMAIN: A program is a list of at most four operations applied left to\nright to input x. inc adds one; dec subtracts one; double multiplies by two; square\nsquares the current value. Find any program realizing the requested polynomial\nidentity for EVERY rational x. A few example matches are not enough. The public\nchecker is tools/check_polynomial.py; it checks the full exact coefficient identity.\nUse python3 tools/check_polynomial.py --program inc,square --coefficients 1,2,1\nas an example of its interface, not as the answer to the task. Optional --x evaluates\nthe same program at a rational input. Do not edit this checker or other tool files.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
